# Working notes are not part of the package and must never be published.
# Chris, 2026-08-29: nothing goes in the public repo that is not
# completely necessary to be there. They live in the private repo instead.
artifacts/
MASTER-PLAN.md
HANDOFF*.md
LANE-*.md
WORK-QUEUE.md

# Session-local editor/agent state. These are written by whatever tool is open
# on the repo, they differ per machine, and `settings.local.json` is where a
# personal server address or an alert token ends up. They are harmless today
# (54 bytes, one key) and that is not the point: they sit untracked in a PUBLIC
# repo, so one `git add -A` publishes whatever they happen to hold that day.
.claude/
.mcp.json
